12: N+1 query problem kya hai?
ans - N+1 query problem occurs when we execute one query to fetch a collection of records and then execute an additional query for each record to fetch its association. This causes unnecessary database queries and performance issues. We can commonly solve it using eager loading such as include

13: N+1 ko kaise solve karoge?
ans - N+1 problem ko solve karne ke liye eager loading use karte hain. Rails mein commonly includes use karte hain, jo associations ko efficiently load karta hai and prevents a separate query for every record. Depending on the requirement, we can also use preload or eager_load.


14: Scope kya hota hai?
ans - Scope ek reusable named query hoti hai jo ActiveRecord model mein commonly-used conditions ko define karti hai.


class User < ApplicationRecord
  scope :active, -> { where(status: "active") }
end

